# Everything a generator writes is marked linguist-generated, which collapses it in a GitHub
# diff and keeps it out of the repository's language statistics. A generated file that is not
# marked shows up as hand-written work in every review, and a regenerated thousand-line CRD
# buries the twenty lines that were actually written.
#
# Grouped by the target that writes them, so this file reads as a list of what each generator
# owns. Check a specific file rather than reasoning about the patterns:
#
#   git check-attr linguist-generated -- controlplane/api/v1alpha1/zz_generated.deepcopy.go

# `go mod vendor`
vendor/** linguist-vendored

# `make generate-deepcopy` (controller-gen object)
**/zz_generated.deepcopy.go linguist-generated

# `make manifests` (controller-gen crd)
bootstrap/config/crd/bases/*.yaml linguist-generated
controlplane/config/crd/bases/*.yaml linguist-generated

# `make manifests` (controller-gen rbac). Only role.yaml: the other five files in each rbac
# directory are hand-written and must stay unmarked.
bootstrap/config/rbac/role.yaml linguist-generated
controlplane/config/rbac/role.yaml linguist-generated

# release-please
CHANGELOG.md linguist-generated
